    "type": "performance",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "model_diff.py loaded each module directly and left collection file handles open across module comparisons.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_480e64a072574c4fb924bb9e708fa642",
          "call_5bcb9fe25b3e412fb674c20207a10123"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "Both branches now bracket module.load with begin_deferred_load/end_deferred_load and close their collection after forwarding and unloading. Completing deferred reads before forward is essential because deferred get_tensor returns destination storage before populating it.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_12752221fd0b421786659b834d03027a",
          "call_5bcb9fe25b3e412fb674c20207a10123"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "The change enables batched loading and bounds handle retention to each branch's module processing. It leaves comparison formulas and device selection unchanged; speed and resource savings are not measured.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_12752221fd0b421786659b834d03027a",
          "call_480e64a072574c4fb924bb9e708fa642"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "Read ancestor entries 25d9388 and 9575f7d: they explain the B-state prefix and final-logit diagnostics respectively. The latter records the perplexity-axis observation retained here.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_189798984a15437999fade547628388e",
          "call_ac55ff1b7da746e482bfa95ba7b1a7da"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "PR #26, \u201cSuperior 3INST parameters,\u201d proposes decoder changes and discusses model_diff.py evaluation. Its relationship to this loading change is only contextual inference from the shared script, not an established fix linkage.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_c03400b8c9f3488581fd187b6a8fc20e",
          "call_45a3c959104641d6a8fbc18817b00a52",
          "call_12752221fd0b421786659b834d03027a"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #7 reports an undefined __cxa_call_terminate import symbol; issue #34 reports a Cholesky failure during quantization. Neither discussion establishes that this script-loading change addresses its reported failure.",
