    ],
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "usage-evaluation",
        "title": "Module-scoped deferred loading and handle release",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "For the default mt_fread loader, eligible get_tensor calls queue destinations and metadata. end_deferred_load groups requests by file and CPU/CUDA destination, sorts by size, and splits work into chunks capped at 2*1024**2 bytes (2 MiB). It then applies temporary-buffer transformations and clears deferred state. Explicit no_defer requests and the Python loader remain immediate.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_5bcb9fe25b3e412fb674c20207a10123"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "close releases populated native handles and sets their entries to None while retaining tensor indexes and headers, allowing later modules to reopen shards. Unlike retaining handles throughout evaluation, this trades potential reopen overhead for earlier release.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_5bcb9fe25b3e412fb674c20207a10123",
              "call_12752221fd0b421786659b834d03027a"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Existing Model._load_single and _load_autosplit guard deferred loading with module.can_defer_load; autosplit also aborts deferred state on exceptions before handling out-of-memory retries. The new script calls omit both the capability guard and recovery. Existing conversion and compilation callers close collections after immediate reads, while Model.load_gen closes after model loading.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_74af6c45fd964861afa360a3baa94815",
              "call_981e77ef842342c1854908b4b4976616",
              "call_12752221fd0b421786659b834d03027a",
              "call_e6322ab78a04464cb9fa58ade0d5ca1d",
              "call_27d90a341b3a4f90ae624609a16c0413",
              "call_2b7d0269a6ff487badfd71c35cb37fed"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [
