        "id": "unguarded-deferred-sliced-load",
        "origin": "authoring_observation",
        "status": "suspected",
        "classification": "defect",
        "description": "Unconditional deferred loading bypasses the existing sliced-module safety guard.",
        "trigger": "A compared module contains a sliced unquantized Linear loaded through the normal weight-key path with mt_fread.",
        "expected_behavior": "Honor can_defer_load and complete immediate reads before load-time copies of sliced weights.",
        "actual_behavior": "Linear.load_fp16 queues the weight, then LinearFP16 copies its still-unpopulated destination into separate storage; end_deferred_load later populates the original destination, not that copy. The inspected reach is the two new main-loop calls when such modules occur, not all models.",
        "locations": [
          {
